Quotas gives each host named a quota by volume, by minutes of use, or
both, on a daily, weekly or monthly cycle. A host is one IPv4 or IPv6
address, or a MAC whose addresses are taken from the firewall's host
discovery. Each is counted once a minute from pf's states - every byte
of its connections, those the coprocessor forwards included where
os-xgs-npu gives pf their counts - and a host over its quota is put in
a pf table that rules of the plugin's block, leaving it DNS and the web
GUI on the firewall, until its cycle starts again. Where os-xgs-npu is
installed its open connections are cut by XGS: Settings' cut list;
without it, at once by the plugin. Off by default.

